# Copy to runpod/.env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPO COMPUTES; IT DOES NOT INGEST.
# A separate system owns every vendor download and fills the SOURCE volume.
# The vendor API tokens below are therefore commented out: nothing here reads
# them, and leaving them live invited a "just one quick fetch" patch. The values
# are preserved (not deleted) in case the download system wants them moved over.
#
# Volumes:
#   RUNPOD_VOLUME_ID   the SOURCE tape (crimtr8kbf) — READ-ONLY, never mounted.
#   CALC_VOLUME_ID     the calc volume (k4cli3aj48) — everything computed here.
# scripts/_common.sh rebinds the mountable volume to CALC and refuses to write
# or mount anything in PROTECTED_VOLUMES.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# One .env, one volume, one set of scripts. Pick the vendor at launch:
#   scripts/launch.sh          # EODHD (default)
#   scripts/launch.sh nasdaq   # Sharadar / Nasdaq Data Link
#   scripts/launch.sh tiingo   # Tiingo (tertiary cross-check)
# Fill in the token(s) for whichever vendor(s) you plan to launch.

# --- EODHD ---
# [download system owns this] EODHD_API_TOKEN=eodhd key

# --- Sharadar (retail API, api.sharadar.com) ---
# Individual/retail subscribers buy the Core US Equities Bundle at https://sharadar.com/subscribe
# (data.nasdaq.com is institutional-only now) and get an api.sharadar.com key. The fetcher calls
# https://api.sharadar.com/v1.0/data/<endpoint> with this key. Only needed for `scripts/launch.sh nasdaq`.
# [download system owns this] SHARADAR_API_KEY=your sharadar.com api key

# --- Tiingo (free tier ok; https://www.tiingo.com/account/api/token) ---
# Tertiary D-12 price cross-check. Only needed for `scripts/launch.sh tiingo`.
# Optional second account: set TIINGO_API_TOKEN2 and the fetcher splits the universe half/half
# (free tier caps 500 unique symbols/month PER account) and interleaves both rate windows.
# [download system owns this] TIINGO_API_TOKEN=your tiingo api token
# TIINGO_API_TOKEN2=second tiingo account token

# --- Logging ---
# When true, fetch.py stores a full run log (data/logs/run-<ts>.log) on the volume on SUCCESS.
# Failures (error-<ts>.log) and crashes (crash-<ts>.log) are ALWAYS logged regardless of this flag.
# [download system owns this] STORE_LOGS=false

# --- RunPod ACCOUNT API key (rpa_...) ---
# Used to CREATE the pod and (passed in as RUNPOD_TERMINATE_KEY) to let the pod
# SELF-TERMINATE. The pod-injected RUNPOD_API_KEY is pod-scoped and 403s on DELETE.
RUNPOD_API_KEY=rpa_xxx

# --- RunPod S3 API keys (Settings -> S3 API Keys) ---
# Used by scripts/_common.sh (and everything sourcing it). aws CLI reads these from the env.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=user_xxx
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=rps_xxx

# --- Network volume ---
# Create a RunPod network volume, then fill these from its details page.
RUNPOD_VOLUME_ID=xxxxxxxxxx
RUNPOD_S3_REGION=eu-ro-1                       # lowercase, for the aws CLI
RUNPOD_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3api-eu-ro-1.runpod.io
RUNPOD_DATACENTER=EU-RO-1                       # uppercase, for pod create (must match the volume's DC)

# --- Pod sizing (optional; defaults shown) ---
# RUNPOD_VCPU=2
# RUNPOD_IMAGE=python:3.11-slim
# CPU flavors launch.sh may rent (default = all). Valid: cpu3c cpu3g cpu3m cpu5c cpu5g cpu5m
# RUNPOD_CPU_FLAVORS=["cpu3c","cpu5c"]
